{"content": "CLAUDIA — URGENT: RESTORE MY COMPLETE RAINBOW GAME, ACTIVATE ALL AGENTS AND SERVICES, ENABLE FIVE-MINUTE GITHUB AUTOSAVE, AND CONTINUE MY APPROVED SCREENS\n\nClaudia, I am switching to this Claude account because it has available usage credits.\n\nTHIS IS MY EXISTING RAINBOW GAME. DO NOT CREATE A NEW PROJECT, RESTART DEVELOPMENT, OR REBUILD WORK THAT HAS ALREADY BEEN COMPLETED.\n\nMy previous Claude account has spent considerable time reconstructing my original approved game screens into real playable 3D Android environments.\n\nI want you to recover everything from GitHub, restore my development environment, activate my specialist agents, reconnect any necessary services, and CONTINUE THE ACTUAL VISUAL IMPROVEMENTS.\n\nDO NOT SPEND MY NEW CLAUDE CREDITS REPEATING SETUP WORK THAT HAS ALREADY BEEN COMPLETED.\n\n---\n\n1. MY EXACT GITHUB REPOSITORY AND BRANCH\n\nRepository:\n\nhttps://github.com/josiahscalia5-dev/rainbow-\n\nBranch from my previous Claude account:\n\n\"ccr-3b139b48-0qqkkz\"\n\nThis is the branch I am giving you to recover my latest work.\n\nFIRST:\n\n1. Connect to my existing GitHub repository.\n2. Fetch the supplied branch and verify its latest commit against GitHub.\n3. Read \"CLAUDE.md\".\n4. Read the newest instructions at the TOP of \"docs/NEW_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_HANDOFF.md\".\n5. Read \"backups/START_NEW_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT.md\".\n6. Read the latest specialist status, coordination documents, and screen-specific progress files.\n7. Inspect \"backups/wip/\" for unfinished work.\n8. Check whether any specialist branch contains newer completed work than the supplied lead branch.\n\nIMPORTANT: My GitHub default branch contains an older version of the project. Do not accidentally restore that old version.\n\nPreserve the supplied branch and existing screen branches.\n\nIf another Claude account might still be working, create a separate continuation branch or worktree from the verified latest appropriate checkpoint rather than overwriting its branch.\n\nDo not merge or overwrite any completed screen without my approval.\n\n---\n\n2. FIRST PRIORITY: ENABLE AUTOMATIC GITHUB SAVING IMMEDIATELY\n\nBEFORE YOU BEGIN NEW DEVELOPMENT, ACTIVATE AND VERIFY FIVE-MINUTE AUTOSAVE.\n\nI do not want to spend the entire session asking whether my work is being saved.\n\nConfigure automatic saving to my existing GitHub repository every five minutes while this Claude development environment is running.\n\nThe saving system must cover:\n\n- The lead development branch.\n- All active specialist-agent branches.\n- Each specialist's separate working directory.\n- Uncommitted work in progress.\n- Screen reconstruction code.\n- 3D models, textures, and materials.\n- Approved images and reference assets.\n- Blender project files.\n- World Labs Marble outputs and downloaded assets.\n- fal.ai-generated reference images.\n- Depth Anything 3 results and scripts.\n- Before-and-after comparison screenshots.\n- Test results, videos, and technical findings.\n- Agent definitions, instructions, progress, and handoff notes.\n- Plugin and server configuration files that are safe to save.\n\nSave unfinished work as clearly labeled WIP checkpoints. Never silently treat unfinished edits as approved changes.\n\nUse Git LFS for large assets.\n\nVerify the LFS objects actually exist remotely rather than merely checking that pointer files were committed.\n\nDo not save API keys, passwords, tokens, or other private credentials into GitHub.\n\nRun an immediate test save and verify the remote commit matches the local checkpoint.\n\nThen keep autosaving every five minutes throughout this active session.\n\nAlso save after every successful visual improvement, before stopping an agent, and at the end of the session.\n\nIf the autosave daemon cannot run when the cloud environment is inactive, tell me that clearly and ensure the latest checkpoint has been pushed before the session ends.\n\nI WANT AUTOSAVE WORKING FROM THE BEGINNING, NOT AFTER HOURS OF DEVELOPMENT.\n\n---\n\n3. RESTORE ALL MY DESIGN AGENTS AND MULTI-AGENT DEVELOPMENT\n\nMy project already has ten specialist-agent definitions.\n\nRestore and verify all ten from \".claude/agents/\".\n\nDo not invent replacement agents when the original definitions are already available.\n\nI want MULTIPLE SPECIALISTS WORKING ON DIFFERENT APPROVED SCREENS AT THE SAME TIME.\n\nRestore the existing screen-specific workstreams for:\n\n- Screen 04 — Through the Five Arrows.\n- Screen 05 — Flow Into the Current.\n- Screen 06 — Crest the Rinse Arch.\n- Screen 07 — Dive the Washer Tube.\n- Screen 08 — Final Spin Chamber.\n\nStart two screen-building specialists concurrently, following the existing project coordination rules. Only increase concurrency if the environment safely supports it without risking work or disrupting other agents.\n\nEvery specialist must:\n\n- Use the latest saved checkpoint for its assigned screen.\n- Work in its own branch and worktree.\n- Preserve successful existing work.\n- Follow my strict approved-artwork instructions.\n- Focus on the biggest visual differences first.\n- Save work frequently to GitHub.\n- Report actual visual improvements.\n- Never claim a screen is approved without my permission.\n\nIf a specialist was stopped when the previous account ran out of credits, restart it from its latest saved checkpoint.\n\nDO NOT MAKE IT START OVER.\n\n---\n\n4. RESTORE AND VERIFY WORLD LABS MARBLE\n\nMy project already uses World Labs Marble.\n\nRestore the existing Marble integration, its relevant plugin or skill, and the existing Image-Blaster workflow where available.\n\nVerify:\n\n- Whether the Marble plugin or skill is installed and enabled.\n- Whether the World Labs API connection works.\n- Which World Labs account the active key belongs to.\n- The account's available API credits, if accessible.\n- Whether existing world IDs are accessible with that particular account.\n- Whether previously generated worlds, splats, meshes, and other assets have been restored from GitHub and Git LFS.\n- Whether the Image-Blaster scripts still work.\n\nMy previous accounts have used more than one World Labs account. Do not assume that a world created under one account is accessible using another account's API key.\n\nDo not overwrite a working key unnecessarily.\n\nIf secure authentication is required, show me the proper credential form.\n\nNEVER ASK ME TO PASTE SECRET API KEYS INTO THE CHAT OR SAVE THEM TO GITHUB.\n\nDo not generate new paid Marble worlds simply to prove that Marble works.\n\nUse the existing saved assets first.\n\n---\n\n5. RESTORE AND VERIFY MY FAL.AI ACCOUNT\n\nI already have a purchased fal.ai account that has been used successfully for this project.\n\nRestore its existing configuration and check that the saved account connection is working.\n\nVerify:\n\n- API authentication.\n- Access to existing completed requests.\n- Access to the previously generated reference images.\n- The existing image-edit workflow.\n- Whether additional reference views can be generated when needed.\n\nDo not replace my existing account with a different account.\n\nIf the API key must be entered again because this is a different Claude account, request it through a secure credential form.\n\nIf the service is already connected and passes a live, non-billed verification, DO NOT ASK ME TO RECONNECT IT.\n\nUse paid image generation only for specific visual reconstruction tasks I authorize. Report costs and avoid duplicate jobs.\n\n---\n\n6. RESTORE DEPTH ANYTHING 3 AND THE OTHER TOOLS\n\nMy previous Claude account successfully tested Depth Anything 3.\n\nThe results, scripts, and findings were saved in:\n\n\"docs/briefs/2026-11-18-r11/DA3_TEST.md\"\n\nand\n\n\"qa/da3/2026-11-18/\"\n\nVerify the latest versions of these records.\n\nRestore Depth Anything 3 if its environment is missing, using the existing installation instructions.\n\nPreserve the commercially compatible model choices already documented.\n\nAlso check the existing availability of:\n\n- Blender.\n- Three.js and WebGL2.\n- Node.js, TypeScript, and Vite.\n- Playwright MCP.\n- Python image tools.\n- ffmpeg.\n- GitHub and Git LFS.\n- Hugging Face.\n- Other project-relevant MCP servers and plugins.\n\nDo not reinstall packages that are already working.\n\nTest only what is necessary to establish that these capabilities are usable.\n\nIf a nonessential plugin is unavailable, record that fact and continue game development instead of spending my credits repeatedly troubleshooting it.\n\n---\n\n7. HUGGING FACE — I ALREADY AUTHORIZED THIS\n\nI previously gave explicit permission to connect Hugging Face and test additional reference views for Screen 04.\n\nPlease respect that decision.\n\nCheck whether Hugging Face is connected to this Claude account.\n\nIf it is already connected, verify access and proceed with the authorized work.\n\nIf a new account authorization is required, provide the actual connection card or exact steps so I can complete it.\n\nDo not repeatedly ask me whether I want Hugging Face.\n\nThe previous research identified Stable Virtual Camera and ViewCrafter as possible tools for additional reference viewpoints.\n\nTheir usefulness for my game has NOT yet been demonstrated.\n\nDo not assume either model can reconstruct my entire 3D game.\n\nUse them only if an accessible, appropriately licensed test can meaningfully help my approved visual reconstruction.\n\nPreserve all original artwork.\n\n---\n\n8. MY MOST IMPORTANT RULE: EXACT APPROVED VISUAL SCREENS\n\nMY ORIGINAL APPROVED SCREENS ARE THE BLUEPRINT.\n\nI do not want Rainbow-inspired environments.\n\nI do not want similar-looking tunnels.\n\nI do not want new scenery.\n\nI WANT MY EXACT APPROVED SCENERY RECREATED AS CLOSELY AS TECHNICALLY POSSIBLE.\n\nThat includes the same:\n\n- Tunnel architecture and depth.\n- Washing-machine walls and mechanisms.\n- Gold rings and metallic details.\n- Cyan-blue, pink, purple, and magenta water.\n- Water thickness, curves, and formations.\n- Foam and bubbles.\n- Lighting and reflections.\n- Characters and backgrounds.\n- Visual proportions and composition.\n\nBenny, my pink fluffy character with his purple-and-white striped beanie and yellow star, must swim naturally THROUGH these actual environments.\n\nThe scenery must remain consistent as he swims.\n\nIt must not suddenly become a flat ramp, generic corridor, disconnected ring tunnel, or completely different environment.\n\nPRIORITY: VISUAL APPEARANCE FIRST.\n\nDo not spend my credits on unrelated gameplay development, new levels, animations beyond what is needed to assess the swimming, or unnecessary camera redesign.\n\nScreens 01–03 and 09–11, which include the cartoon girl and cinematic sequences, are for Google Flow. Do not rebuild them as playable 3D.\n\nFocus on the five playable screens: 04–08.\n\nMy minimum goal is 8.5/10 visual resemblance during gameplay, ideally 9–9.5/10.\n\nDo not promise those results until the real game proves them.\n\n---\n\n9. CONTINUE FROM THE LATEST VISUAL PROGRESS\n\nRead the newest handoff and specialist reports instead of assuming these notes are the final checkpoint.\n\nThe last work I know about includes:\n\nScreen 05: Improving the torn S-shaped river, its far transition, and distorted water and scenery.\n\nScreen 08: Improving the near water, chamber seams, and remaining mismatched visual details.\n\nScreen 06: Two bent-tunnel experiments were rejected because they did not improve the overall scenery. Preserve the previously kept version. Do not repeat those failed experiments without a genuinely different, justified solution.\n\nScreen 04: Additional reference views V04-1 and V04-2 were generated. Their ability to improve the actual playable scenery was still being tested.\n\nScreen 07: Existing progress and specialist instructions must be restored for continuation.\n\nUse the most recent verified progress for each screen, not an outdated summary.\n\nContinue from whatever the previous Claude account last saved.\n\n---\n\n10. SHOW ME REAL VISUAL PROOF\n\nFor each meaningful improvement, provide separate full-size portrait images:\n\n1. ORIGINAL APPROVED SCREEN\n\n2. BEFORE — PREVIOUS GAME VERSION\n\n3. NEW — CORRECTED REAL GAME VERSION\n\nDo not combine them into a tiny collage for my final review.\n\nAlso evaluate the beginning, middle, end, and relevant turns during actual gameplay.\n\nEvery visual result must receive one clear verdict:\n\nGOOD IMPROVEMENT\n\nNOT AN IMPROVEMENT\n\nNOT YET PROVEN\n\nTell me exactly what improved and what remains different.\n\nDo not use color percentages alone as evidence of visual resemblance.\n\nDo not approve anything on my behalf.\n\n---\n\n11. VERIFY EVERYTHING ONCE, THEN START BUILDING\n\nWhen this Claude session begins, I expect you to:\n\nFIRST: Restore my latest GitHub work and activate five-minute autosave.\n\nSECOND: Verify that GitHub, Git LFS, the specialist agents, Marble World Labs, fal.ai, Hugging Face where available, Depth Anything 3, and necessary development tools are operational.\n\nTHIRD: Restore active specialist workstreams and begin meaningful visual reconstruction immediately.\n\nFOURTH: Give me one concise startup report that clearly states:\n\n- Which GitHub branch and commit you recovered.\n- Whether five-minute autosave was tested successfully.\n- Whether the large assets are intact.\n- How many specialist agents are actually running.\n- Which screens those agents are improving.\n- Which services are verified working.\n- Which connections genuinely need my action.\n- What specific visual improvements are being worked on.\n\nDo not claim a plugin is installed, connected, enabled, or working unless you actually verified it.\n\nDo not claim specialist agents are running unless their sessions are actually active.\n\nAFTER THAT, STOP REPEATING SETUP AND CONTINUE BUILDING MY APPROVED SCREENS.\n\n---\n\n12. FINAL INSTRUCTION\n\nClaudia, I'm switching accounts because I want to keep making progress, not because I want to restart everything.\n\nSAVE FIRST. RESTORE EVERYTHING. ACTIVATE THE AGENTS. VERIFY THE SERVICES. THEN BUILD.\n\nI want all five playable Rainbow screens to become faithful 3D reconstructions of my original approved artwork.\n\nNo redesigns.\n\nNo generic scenery.\n\nNo wasted credits repeating completed work.\n\nNo false progress reports.\n\nContinue automatically from the latest safe checkpoint whenever authorization is not required.\n\nSTART BY ENABLING AND TESTING FIVE-MINUTE GITHUB AUTOSAVE. THEN GET MY MULTIPLE SCREEN SPECIALISTS WORKING AGAIN AND CONTINUE THE ACTUAL VISUAL RECONSTRUCTION.\n\nDo not stop after giving me a setup plan. Perform the available steps in this session and show me the verified results.", "operation": "enqueue", "sessionId": "165d9785-b934-5127-ba04-3006ec07d851", "timestamp": "2026-11-18T12:32:33.929Z", "type": "queue-operation"}
{"content": "CLAUDIA — ACTIVATE MY AI TOOLS, STOP WASTING CREDITS, AND CONTINUE REBUILDING MY EXACT APPROVED SCREENS\n\nClaudia, I want you to take this instruction seriously and apply it immediately.\n\nMy number-one priority is recreating my ORIGINAL APPROVED Rainbow game screens as accurately as technically possible, with Benny swimming naturally through the actual scenery.\n\nDO NOT REDESIGN MY SCREENS OR REPLACE THEM WITH DIFFERENT ENVIRONMENTS.\n\n1. HUGGING FACE — I ALREADY SAID YES\n\nI already authorized connecting Hugging Face and conducting the Screen 04 reference-view test.\n\nDo not ask me for the same permission repeatedly.\n\nCheck whether Hugging Face is already connected to this Claude account.\n\nIf the connector requires me to complete authentication, show me the actual connection card or exact authorization steps.\n\nIf direct access already works, do not waste time installing an unnecessary connector.\n\nCheck whether Stable Virtual Camera or ViewCrafter is actually available through a usable GPU service and whether its license permits the intended use.\n\nOnly conduct a targeted test if you can access the model.\n\nIMPORTANT: I WANT TO SEE WHETHER THE GENERATED VIEWS IMPROVE MY ACTUAL 3D GAME, NOT JUST WHETHER THEY PRODUCE MORE PRETTY PICTURES.\n\nUse my existing Screen 04 reference images and test whether a consistent sequence of approved-looking viewpoints can be incorporated into the playable scene.\n\nIf this method doesn't improve the real game, reject it and continue with the existing reconstruction method.\n\n2. WORLD LABS MARBLE\n\nVerify that World Labs Marble and the existing Image-Blaster workflow are available.\n\nConfirm the API account and key work and that existing assets are accessible.\n\nPreserve all previously generated Marble assets, world data, meshes, splats, and reference materials.\n\nDo not repeat expensive Marble generation or restart completed work.\n\nDo not assume a world from one account can be accessed with a different account's key.\n\nIf authentication is required, use the proper secure credential form.\n\n3. FAL.AI\n\nVerify that my existing purchased fal.ai account is connected and functioning.\n\nUse the saved successful requests and previously generated reference views.\n\nDo not repeat the eight-image Screen 04 pilot. It has already been completed.\n\nOnly generate additional images when there is a specific, justified need to improve an approved screen.\n\nNo duplicate paid jobs, unnecessary API testing, or wasted credits.\n\n4. DEPTH ANYTHING 3\n\nDepth Anything 3 has already been installed and tested in a previous session.\n\nRead the saved findings.\n\nUse its depth estimates as supporting measurements for the actual geometry, particularly Screens 04, 06, and 07.\n\nDo not repeat the entire installation or earlier research.\n\nDo not treat depth maps as finished scenery or assume the model is always correct.\n\n5. ALL OTHER PLUGINS AND MCP SERVERS\n\nCheck the existing project configuration and verify the tools that genuinely contribute to visual reconstruction.\n\nThat includes Blender, Three.js, Playwright, the existing design-agent definitions, and other relevant installed capabilities.\n\nDo not spend hours searching plugin stores or reinstalling tools.\n\nIf a genuinely new, accessible AI capability offers a significant advantage for reconstructing my exact scenery, tell me:\n\n- Its name.\n- Whether it is installed and usable.\n- Which specific visual defect it can address.\n- Why it is more effective than our current approach.\n- Whether it costs money.\n\nIf it does not demonstrably help, do not install it.\n\nI AM BUILDING THIS GAME MYSELF WITH AI. DO NOT RECOMMEND HIRING DEVELOPERS OR ARTISTS.\n\n6. MULTIPLE DESIGN AGENTS MUST KEEP BUILDING\n\nKeep my Screen 05 and Screen 08 specialists working simultaneously.\n\nContinue the existing Screen 04 reconstruction test without restarting completed work.\n\nQueue Screen 07 and the remaining Screen 06 reconstruction work for the next appropriate slots.\n\nScreen 06's two failed tunnel-bending attempts must remain rejected.\n\nAll specialists must work from the latest GitHub checkpoints.\n\n7. FIX THE ACTUAL VISUAL PROBLEMS\n\nSCREEN 04: Rebuild the correct washer opening, five glowing arrows, thick colorful water, gold structure, foam, bubbles, and scenery.\n\nSCREEN 05: Fix the torn water, S-shaped river, distorted tunnel, and incorrect scenery near the level transition.\n\nSCREEN 06: Reconstruct the actual approved sweeping water crest and continuous purple-and-gold tunnel together, not a collection of disconnected gold hoops.\n\nSCREEN 07: Preserve my approved purple-and-gold washer-tube environment throughout the plunge.\n\nSCREEN 08: Preserve the approved chamber and correct the water smears, seams, and remaining mismatched scenery.\n\nVISUAL SCENERY FIRST. DO NOT WORK ON UNRELATED FEATURES.\n\n8. PROVE THE IMPROVEMENTS\n\nFor each meaningful correction, show three separate full-size images:\n\n1. ORIGINAL APPROVED\n2. BEFORE\n3. NEW REAL GAME RENDER\n\nTest how the scenery appears while Benny actually swims through it.\n\nReport one clear verdict:\n\nGOOD IMPROVEMENT — KEEP IT.\n\nNOT AN IMPROVEMENT — REJECT IT.\n\nNOT YET PROVEN — CONTINUE THE TARGETED TEST.\n\nMy minimum goal is 8.5/10 visual resemblance throughout gameplay, ideally 9–9.5/10.\n\nDo not exaggerate ratings or declare success without proof.\n\nNothing is approved until I personally approve it.\n\n9. FIVE-MINUTE GITHUB AUTOSAVE\n\nImmediately verify that automatic saving is enabled.\n\nEvery five minutes while the session is active, save the lead branch, specialist work, unfinished edits, relevant assets, and progress to my existing GitHub repository.\n\nPreserve each specialist's separate branch and worktree.\n\nVerify that the remote saves succeed.\n\nNever put private API credentials into GitHub.\n\n10. FINAL INSTRUCTION — STOP SETTING UP AND START BUILDING\n\nI do not want another session consumed by installation, research, and repeated checks.\n\nVERIFY EXISTING SERVICES ONCE. CONNECT ONLY WHAT IS NECESSARY. RESTORE MY AGENTS. KEEP BUILDING.\n\nDo not stop my current specialists merely to respond to this message.\n\nDo not restart finished work.\n\nDo not spend credits repeating previous experiments.\n\nFocus on the biggest visual differences first.\n\nMy original approved Screens 04–08 must remain the design blueprints.\n\nScreens involving the cartoon girl remain assigned to Google Flow.\n\nI WANT REAL PROGRESS TOWARD MY EXACT APPROVED SCREENS, WITH BENNY SWIMMING NATURALLY THROUGH THEM. NOTHING DIFFERENT.\n\nContinue the current visual reconstruction and show me the next genuine improvement.", "operation": "enqueue", "sessionId": "165d9785-b934-5127-ba04-3006ec07d851", "timestamp": "2026-11-18T12:32:33.990Z", "type": "queue-operation"}
