{"clientPlatform": "android", "cwd": "/home/user/rainbow-", "entrypoint": "remote_mobile", "gitBranch": "ccr-e908f8da-cy4yc1", "isSidechain": false, "mergedSendUuids": ["7f5d4791-a8de-4c8b-8e93-a36bb6557539"], "message": {"content": "CLAUDIA — URGENT: RESTORE MY COMPLETE RAINBOW GAME, ACTIVATE ALL AGENTS AND SERVICES, ENABLE FIVE-MINUTE GITHUB AUTOSAVE, AND CONTINUE MY APPROVED SCREENS\n\nClaudia, I am switching to this Claude account because it has available usage credits.\n\nTHIS IS MY EXISTING RAINBOW GAME. DO NOT CREATE A NEW PROJECT, RESTART DEVELOPMENT, OR REBUILD WORK THAT HAS ALREADY BEEN COMPLETED.\n\nMy previous Claude account has spent considerable time reconstructing my original approved game screens into real playable 3D Android environments.\n\nI want you to recover everything from GitHub, restore my development environment, activate my specialist agents, reconnect any necessary services, and CONTINUE THE ACTUAL VISUAL IMPROVEMENTS.\n\nDO NOT SPEND MY NEW CLAUDE CREDITS REPEATING SETUP WORK THAT HAS ALREADY BEEN COMPLETED.\n\n---\n\n1. MY EXACT GITHUB REPOSITORY AND BRANCH\n\nRepository:\n\nhttps://github.com/josiahscalia5-dev/rainbow-\n\nBranch from my previous Claude account:\n\n\"ccr-3b139b48-0qqkkz\"\n\nThis is the branch I am giving you to recover my latest work.\n\nFIRST:\n\n1. Connect to my existing GitHub repository.\n2. Fetch the supplied branch and verify its latest commit against GitHub.\n3. Read \"CLAUDE.md\".\n4. Read the newest instructions at the TOP of \"docs/NEW_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_HANDOFF.md\".\n5. Read \"backups/START_NEW_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT.md\".\n6. Read the latest specialist status, coordination documents, and screen-specific progress files.\n7. Inspect \"backups/wip/\" for unfinished work.\n8. Check whether any specialist branch contains newer completed work than the supplied lead branch.\n\nIMPORTANT: My GitHub default branch contains an older version of the project. Do not accidentally restore that old version.\n\nPreserve the supplied branch and existing screen branches.\n\nIf another Claude account might still be working, create a separate continuation branch or worktree from the verified latest appropriate checkpoint rather than overwriting its branch.\n\nDo not merge or overwrite any completed screen without my approval.\n\n---\n\n2. FIRST PRIORITY: ENABLE AUTOMATIC GITHUB SAVING IMMEDIATELY\n\nBEFORE YOU BEGIN NEW DEVELOPMENT, ACTIVATE AND VERIFY FIVE-MINUTE AUTOSAVE.\n\nI do not want to spend the entire session asking whether my work is being saved.\n\nConfigure automatic saving to my existing GitHub repository every five minutes while this Claude development environment is running.\n\nThe saving system must cover:\n\n- The lead development branch.\n- All active specialist-agent branches.\n- Each specialist's separate working directory.\n- Uncommitted work in progress.\n- Screen reconstruction code.\n- 3D models, textures, and materials.\n- Approved images and reference assets.\n- Blender project files.\n- World Labs Marble outputs and downloaded assets.\n- fal.ai-generated reference images.\n- Depth Anything 3 results and scripts.\n- Before-and-after comparison screenshots.\n- Test results, videos, and technical findings.\n- Agent definitions, instructions, progress, and handoff notes.\n- Plugin and server configuration files that are safe to save.\n\nSave unfinished work as clearly labeled WIP checkpoints. Never silently treat unfinished edits as approved changes.\n\nUse Git LFS for large assets.\n\nVerify the LFS objects actually exist remotely rather than merely checking that pointer files were committed.\n\nDo not save API keys, passwords, tokens, or other private credentials into GitHub.\n\nRun an immediate test save and verify the remote commit matches the local checkpoint.\n\nThen keep autosaving every five minutes throughout this active session.\n\nAlso save after every successful visual improvement, before stopping an agent, and at the end of the session.\n\nIf the autosave daemon cannot run when the cloud environment is inactive, tell me that clearly and ensure the latest checkpoint has been pushed before the session ends.\n\nI WANT AUTOSAVE WORKING FROM THE BEGINNING, NOT AFTER HOURS OF DEVELOPMENT.\n\n---\n\n3. RESTORE ALL MY DESIGN AGENTS AND MULTI-AGENT DEVELOPMENT\n\nMy project already has ten specialist-agent definitions.\n\nRestore and verify all ten from \".claude/agents/\".\n\nDo not invent replacement agents when the original definitions are already available.\n\nI want MULTIPLE SPECIALISTS WORKING ON DIFFERENT APPROVED SCREENS AT THE SAME TIME.\n\nRestore the existing screen-specific workstreams for:\n\n- Screen 04 — Through the Five Arrows.\n- Screen 05 — Flow Into the Current.\n- Screen 06 — Crest the Rinse Arch.\n- Screen 07 — Dive the Washer Tube.\n- Screen 08 — Final Spin Chamber.\n\nStart two screen-building specialists concurrently, following the existing project coordination rules. Only increase concurrency if the environment safely supports it without risking work or disrupting other agents.\n\nEvery specialist must:\n\n- Use the latest saved checkpoint for its assigned screen.\n- Work in its own branch and worktree.\n- Preserve successful existing work.\n- Follow my strict approved-artwork instructions.\n- Focus on the biggest visual differences first.\n- Save work frequently to GitHub.\n- Report actual visual improvements.\n- Never claim a screen is approved without my permission.\n\nIf a specialist was stopped when the previous account ran out of credits, restart it from its latest saved checkpoint.\n\nDO NOT MAKE IT START OVER.\n\n---\n\n4. RESTORE AND VERIFY WORLD LABS MARBLE\n\nMy project already uses World Labs Marble.\n\nRestore the existing Marble integration, its relevant plugin or skill, and the existing Image-Blaster workflow where available.\n\nVerify:\n\n- Whether the Marble plugin or skill is installed and enabled.\n- Whether the World Labs API connection works.\n- Which World Labs account the active key belongs to.\n- The account's available API credits, if accessible.\n- Whether existing world IDs are accessible with that particular account.\n- Whether previously generated worlds, splats, meshes, and other assets have been restored from GitHub and Git LFS.\n- Whether the Image-Blaster scripts still work.\n\nMy previous accounts have used more than one World Labs account. Do not assume that a world created under one account is accessible using another account's API key.\n\nDo not overwrite a working key unnecessarily.\n\nIf secure authentication is required, show me the proper credential form.\n\nNEVER ASK ME TO PASTE SECRET API KEYS INTO THE CHAT OR SAVE THEM TO GITHUB.\n\nDo not generate new paid Marble worlds simply to prove that Marble works.\n\nUse the existing saved assets first.\n\n---\n\n5. RESTORE AND VERIFY MY FAL.AI ACCOUNT\n\nI already have a purchased fal.ai account that has been used successfully for this project.\n\nRestore its existing configuration and check that the saved account connection is working.\n\nVerify:\n\n- API authentication.\n- Access to existing completed requests.\n- Access to the previously generated reference images.\n- The existing image-edit workflow.\n- Whether additional reference views can be generated when needed.\n\nDo not replace my existing account with a different account.\n\nIf the API key must be entered again because this is a different Claude account, request it through a secure credential form.\n\nIf the service is already connected and passes a live, non-billed verification, DO NOT ASK ME TO RECONNECT IT.\n\nUse paid image generation only for specific visual reconstruction tasks I authorize. Report costs and avoid duplicate jobs.\n\n---\n\n6. RESTORE DEPTH ANYTHING 3 AND THE OTHER TOOLS\n\nMy previous Claude account successfully tested Depth Anything 3.\n\nThe results, scripts, and findings were saved in:\n\n\"docs/briefs/2026-11-18-r11/DA3_TEST.md\"\n\nand\n\n\"qa/da3/2026-11-18/\"\n\nVerify the latest versions of these records.\n\nRestore Depth Anything 3 if its environment is missing, using the existing installation instructions.\n\nPreserve the commercially compatible model choices already documented.\n\nAlso check the existing availability of:\n\n- Blender.\n- Three.js and WebGL2.\n- Node.js, TypeScript, and Vite.\n- Playwright MCP.\n- Python image tools.\n- ffmpeg.\n- GitHub and Git LFS.\n- Hugging Face.\n- Other project-relevant MCP servers and plugins.\n\nDo not reinstall packages that are already working.\n\nTest only what is necessary to establish that these capabilities are usable.\n\nIf a nonessential plugin is unavailable, record that fact and continue game development instead of spending my credits repeatedly troubleshooting it.\n\n---\n\n7. HUGGING FACE — I ALREADY AUTHORIZED THIS\n\nI previously gave explicit permission to connect Hugging Face and test additional reference views for Screen 04.\n\nPlease respect that decision.\n\nCheck whether Hugging Face is connected to this Claude account.\n\nIf it is already connected, verify access and proceed with the authorized work.\n\nIf a new account authorization is required, provide the actual connection card or exact steps so I can complete it.\n\nDo not repeatedly ask me whether I want Hugging Face.\n\nThe previous research identified Stable Virtual Camera and ViewCrafter as possible tools for additional reference viewpoints.\n\nTheir usefulness for my game has NOT yet been demonstrated.\n\nDo not assume either model can reconstruct my entire 3D game.\n\nUse them only if an accessible, appropriately licensed test can meaningfully help my approved visual reconstruction.\n\nPreserve all original artwork.\n\n---\n\n8. MY MOST IMPORTANT RULE: EXACT APPROVED VISUAL SCREENS\n\nMY ORIGINAL APPROVED SCREENS ARE THE BLUEPRINT.\n\nI do not want Rainbow-inspired environments.\n\nI do not want similar-looking tunnels.\n\nI do not want new scenery.\n\nI WANT MY EXACT APPROVED SCENERY RECREATED AS CLOSELY AS TECHNICALLY POSSIBLE.\